NEU-DET-corrected — LICENSE
===========================

This file covers TWO different things. Please read both parts.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART 1 — The modifications made in this release
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The changes made to produce "NEU-DET-corrected" are released under the

    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0)

Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

These modifications are:

  * removal of 1 duplicate image (patches_105.jpg, pixel-identical to
    patches_101.jpg),
  * removal of 3 duplicated bounding boxes (one box listed twice verbatim in
    each of crazing_120, inclusion_62, patches_198),
  * addition of a seeded, class-stratified train/val/test split,
  * conversion of the annotations to YOLO format alongside the original
    Pascal VOC format,
  * regeneration of classes.txt, data.yaml, ImageSets/ and this documentation.

You are free to share and adapt these modifications for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART 2 — The underlying NEU-DET data (IMPORTANT)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The underlying images and annotations originate from the NEU Surface Defect
Database (NEU-DET):

    Song, Kechen; Yan, Yunhui.
    "A noise robust method based on completed local binary patterns for
    hot-rolled steel strip surface defects."
    Applied Surface Science 285:858-864, 2013.
    DOI: 10.1016/j.apsusc.2013.08.123

    He, Yu; Song, Kechen; Meng, Qinggang; Yan, Yunhui.
    "An End-to-end Steel Surface Defect Detection Approach via Fusing
    Multiple Hierarchical Features."
    IEEE Transactions on Instrumentation and Measurement 69(4):1493-1504, 2020.
    DOI: 10.1109/TIM.2019.2915404

    Official page: https://faculty.neu.edu.cn/songkc/en/zdylm/263265/

THE ORIGINAL AUTHORS HAVE NOT STATED A LICENSE FOR THE DATASET.

  * The dataset is distributed by the authors (Google Drive / Baidu Netdisk)
    for research use, with a request to cite the papers above.
  * No LICENSE file, no licence statement, and no terms of use are provided
    with the download.
  * The associated papers are published by Elsevier / IEEE; those licences
    cover the ARTICLES, and do not by themselves license the dataset.

Consequently, the copyright status of the underlying NEU-DET images and
annotations is UNDETERMINED. No licence is granted for them by this file.

>>> Before any commercial use or redistribution of the image data, you must
>>> determine the applicable terms from the original authors.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If you are the rights holder of NEU-DET and would like this release changed or
removed, please open an issue and it will be actioned promptly.
